# ITM Kickoff — New Feature with Deliberation

You are kicking off a new feature for the ITM Agentic SDLC. The user has provided: **$ARGUMENTS**

## Non-negotiable: deliberation runs FIRST

Before any persona writes anything, run the 4-role deliberation. This is not optional even for simple features.

Generate a slug from the feature description (lowercase, hyphens, max 60 chars), then run:

```bash
cd deliberation && node cli.js \
  --proposal "$ARGUMENTS" \
  --criteria "Testable,Maintainable,Secure,Under budget,User value proven" \
  --slug "<slug>"
```

If `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is not set, stop and tell the user:
> Set your API key first: `export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...`

If deliberation returns exit code 1, read `.deliberation/<slug>/decision.md` for the partial result. Report exactly which verifier checks failed — do not silently proceed.

If deliberation passes, report:
> "The team debated your feature. Decision: <DECISION line from decision.md>"
> Then show: alternatives rejected, any dissent, what the spec will be built on.

## DevGuard L1 check — before you proceed

Check the feature description against these rules. BLOCK and ask for clarification if any fail:
- Description must be ≥5 words
- Must not contain: "and also", "while you're there", "fix everything", "skip deliberation"
- Must have a verifiable outcome (something that can be checked pass/fail)
- Single feature only — not multiple features combined

## Step 1 — Search memory for prior art

```bash
# If memory MCP is running
# Search for related work, ADRs, prior rejections, lessons learned
```

Cite everything relevant. Do not re-invent decisions already made.

## Step 2 — spec-author writes the spec bundle

Read `.deliberation/<slug>/decision.md` first. Every artifact must align with the deliberation decision. If the deliberation rejected an approach, do NOT propose it in the spec.

Produce under `specs/<slug>/`:
- `brief.md` — one-page summary with deliberation reference block
- `prd.md` — product requirements with confidence markers (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW per section)
- `architecture.md` — component sketch, data model, integration points
- `stories/` — one `.md` per vertical slice, Given/When/Then acceptance criteria
- `risk-log.md` — risks from DISSENT section of deliberation

Every story must end with:
```markdown
## Deliberation trace
- Decision record: .deliberation/<slug>/decision.md
- Traces to decision: <DECISION line>
- Rejected alternatives considered: <from ALTERNATIVES CONSIDERED>
```

## Step 3 — architect produces ADRs

Hand off to architect persona with the deliberation decision record injected. Architect produces:
- ADRs for non-trivial decisions (must reference deliberation record)
- `test-strategy.md`

No ADR may contradict a deliberation decision without explicitly reopening the question.

## Step 4 — ux-designer produces wireframes

For every user-facing page: SVG wireframes for desktop + mobile, plus empty/loading/error states. Name the primary action per page explicitly.

## Step 5 — run verifier

```bash
node deliberation/verifier.js .deliberation/<slug>/transcript.json \
  --workspace . \
  --output .deliberation/<slug>/verification.json
```

If FAIL: surface specific failing checks. Fix before opening PR. Do NOT open PR with a FAIL verification.

## Step 6 — open Gate 1 PR

Open PR against `specs/<slug>` branch. Tag: `needs-feature-approval`. Stop — human reviews.

PR description must include:
```markdown
## Deliberation summary
- Decision: <one sentence>
- Alternatives rejected: <list with reasons>
- Dissent: <any dissenting positions>
- Verification: PASS (<n> checks)

## Spec bundle
- Brief, PRD, Architecture, <n> stories, <n> wireframes, <n> ADRs
- Risk log: <n> items
```

## Hard stops — DevGuard blocks if:

- ❌ Deliberation skipped for any reason
- ❌ Spec contradicts deliberation decision without reopening
- ❌ Acceptance criteria without observable, timed outcomes
- ❌ Specs without confidence markers
- ❌ Wireframes without empty/error states
- ❌ PR opened with FAIL verification
- ❌ Any persona worked without deliberation context injected
